# వనమయూరము · vanamayuramu — prosodic grammar (vrutta, 4 lines, 14 aksharas per line)
# generated from meter_rules.yaml by indic_meter_dawg; do not edit by hand
#
# One grammar, three forms: (1) hierarchical, for reading; (2) right-linear, the same language flattened;
# (3) strict, one symbol per production = the prosodic automaton. All three generate exactly the same poems.
#
# Terminals: U = guru (2 matras), I = laghu (1 matra), ⏎ = line separator.
# Nonterminals: Poem, Unit, Line_<slot>, gana classes (Surya, Indra, Kanda, M4 …), ganas (భ, ర, …).
#   Kanda−జ  = the class minus జ (a constraint removed it)   Kanda=జ|నల = only జ or నల allowed
#   Kanda$U  = only members ending in a guru                   X⟨U⟩ = inside the branch where every line starts with U
#   L2.G3    = line 2, about to read gana 3 (forms 2 and 3)
#   A_UUI_2  = inside alternative UUI of A, 2 symbols already read (form 3 only)

# ===== 1. Hierarchical: Poem → lines → gana classes → ganas → symbols
# poem
Poem → Line ⏎ Line ⏎ Line ⏎ Line                 # 4 lines

# lines
Line → భ జ స న గా                                # slot all: 5 ganas

# ganas → symbols
భ → U I I                                        # bha, 4 matras
జ → I U I                                        # ja, 4 matras
స → I I U                                        # sa, 4 matras
న → I I I                                        # na, 3 matras
గా → U U                                         # gaa, 4 matras

# ===== 2. Right-linear (A → wB | w) over {U, I, ⏎}: the hierarchy flattened
Poem → UII L1.G2
L1.G2 → IUI L1.G3
L1.G3 → IIU L1.G4
L1.G4 → III L1.G5
L1.G5 → UU⏎ L2.G1
L2.G1 → UII L2.G2
L2.G2 → IUI L2.G3
L2.G3 → IIU L2.G4
L2.G4 → III L2.G5
L2.G5 → UU⏎ L3.G1
L3.G1 → UII L3.G2
L3.G2 → IUI L3.G3
L3.G3 → IIU L3.G4
L3.G4 → III L3.G5
L3.G5 → UU⏎ L4.G1
L4.G1 → UII L4.G2
L4.G2 → IUI L4.G3
L4.G3 → IIU L4.G4
L4.G4 → III L4.G5
L4.G5 → UU

# ===== 3. Strict (A → aB | a): 59 productions, 60 states;
# minimized prosodic automaton: 60 states. Every production is commented.
Poem → U Poem_UII_1             # భ bha: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
Poem_UII_1 → I Poem_UII_2       # భ bha: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
Poem_UII_2 → I L1.G2            # భ bha: symbol 3/3, complete → L1.G2
L1.G2 → I L1.G2_IUI_1           # జ ja: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L1.G2_IUI_1 → U L1.G2_IUI_2     # జ ja: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L1.G2_IUI_2 → I L1.G3           # జ ja: symbol 3/3, complete → L1.G3
L1.G3 → I L1.G3_IIU_1           # స sa: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L1.G3_IIU_1 → I L1.G3_IIU_2     # స sa: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L1.G3_IIU_2 → U L1.G4           # స sa: symbol 3/3, complete → L1.G4
L1.G4 → I L1.G4_III_1           # న na: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L1.G4_III_1 → I L1.G4_III_2     # న na: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L1.G4_III_2 → I L1.G5           # న na: symbol 3/3, complete → L1.G5
L1.G5 → U L1.G5_UUNL_1          # గా gaa: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L1.G5_UUNL_1 → U L1.G5_UUNL_2   # గా gaa: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L1.G5_UUNL_2 → ⏎ L2.G1          # గా gaa: symbol 3/3, complete → L2.G1
L2.G1 → U L2.G1_UII_1           # భ bha: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L2.G1_UII_1 → I L2.G1_UII_2     # భ bha: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L2.G1_UII_2 → I L2.G2           # భ bha: symbol 3/3, complete → L2.G2
L2.G2 → I L2.G2_IUI_1           # జ ja: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L2.G2_IUI_1 → U L2.G2_IUI_2     # జ ja: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L2.G2_IUI_2 → I L2.G3           # జ ja: symbol 3/3, complete → L2.G3
L2.G3 → I L2.G3_IIU_1           # స sa: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L2.G3_IIU_1 → I L2.G3_IIU_2     # స sa: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L2.G3_IIU_2 → U L2.G4           # స sa: symbol 3/3, complete → L2.G4
L2.G4 → I L2.G4_III_1           # న na: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L2.G4_III_1 → I L2.G4_III_2     # న na: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L2.G4_III_2 → I L2.G5           # న na: symbol 3/3, complete → L2.G5
L2.G5 → U L2.G5_UUNL_1          # గా gaa: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L2.G5_UUNL_1 → U L2.G5_UUNL_2   # గా gaa: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L2.G5_UUNL_2 → ⏎ L3.G1          # గా gaa: symbol 3/3, complete → L3.G1
L3.G1 → U L3.G1_UII_1           # భ bha: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L3.G1_UII_1 → I L3.G1_UII_2     # భ bha: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L3.G1_UII_2 → I L3.G2           # భ bha: symbol 3/3, complete → L3.G2
L3.G2 → I L3.G2_IUI_1           # జ ja: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L3.G2_IUI_1 → U L3.G2_IUI_2     # జ ja: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L3.G2_IUI_2 → I L3.G3           # జ ja: symbol 3/3, complete → L3.G3
L3.G3 → I L3.G3_IIU_1           # స sa: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L3.G3_IIU_1 → I L3.G3_IIU_2     # స sa: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L3.G3_IIU_2 → U L3.G4           # స sa: symbol 3/3, complete → L3.G4
L3.G4 → I L3.G4_III_1           # న na: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L3.G4_III_1 → I L3.G4_III_2     # న na: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L3.G4_III_2 → I L3.G5           # న na: symbol 3/3, complete → L3.G5
L3.G5 → U L3.G5_UUNL_1          # గా gaa: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L3.G5_UUNL_1 → U L3.G5_UUNL_2   # గా gaa: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L3.G5_UUNL_2 → ⏎ L4.G1          # గా gaa: symbol 3/3, complete → L4.G1
L4.G1 → U L4.G1_UII_1           # భ bha: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L4.G1_UII_1 → I L4.G1_UII_2     # భ bha: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L4.G1_UII_2 → I L4.G2           # భ bha: symbol 3/3, complete → L4.G2
L4.G2 → I L4.G2_IUI_1           # జ ja: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L4.G2_IUI_1 → U L4.G2_IUI_2     # జ ja: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L4.G2_IUI_2 → I L4.G3           # జ ja: symbol 3/3, complete → L4.G3
L4.G3 → I L4.G3_IIU_1           # స sa: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L4.G3_IIU_1 → I L4.G3_IIU_2     # స sa: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L4.G3_IIU_2 → U L4.G4           # స sa: symbol 3/3, complete → L4.G4
L4.G4 → I L4.G4_III_1           # న na: symbol 1/3 read, 2 to go
L4.G4_III_1 → I L4.G4_III_2     # న na: symbol 2/3 read, 1 to go
L4.G4_III_2 → I L4.G5           # న na: symbol 3/3, complete → L4.G5
L4.G5 → U L4.G5_UU_1            # గా gaa: symbol 1/2 read, 1 to go
L4.G5_UU_1 → U                  # గా gaa: symbol 2/2, complete, line ends
